{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789457480,"nonce":"DXK+T7Fowh6owLYvLfhU+m4O6k0=","title":"Dominators were recomputed from scratch with sets, cubic in the blocks","message":"`osr::blocks_dominated_by` built the full dominator sets by the naive iteration (every block starts dominated by all, intersect predecessors to a fixed point), O(blocks^2) per iteration with HashSet intersections, and was called once per loop header in `osr_layout` and once per self-referential phi incoming in SSA construction (`edge_is_back`). A function with a few hundred blocks paid seconds.\n\nMeasured on bench_tokenize once the dict functions grew: Cranelift codegen phase 920 ms, of which nearly all was `blocks_dominated_by` under `osr_layout`; on the previous builtins the same phase was ~150 ms and nbody's compile 58 ms.\n\nFix: `osr::Dominators` computes immediate dominators once by the iterative algorithm over a reverse postorder (Cooper, Harvey, Kennedy), linear in practice, and answers `dominates` by walking the tree. Unreachable blocks keep the old meaning (dominated by everything) so an orphan predecessor never turns a back edge into a forward one. After: tokenize codegen 33 ms, nbody compile 29 ms, pipeline compile 230 to 77 ms.\n\nStill owed: callers compute `Dominators` per query; `osr_layout` could compute it once per function and `edge_is_back` once per phi-filling pass, if the SSA builder's CFG is stable between the calls.","files":null}]}